# The build context is this directory, and `.venv` alone is hundreds of
# megabytes of the wrong interpreter's packages. Nothing here is COPYied by
# the Dockerfile; excluding it keeps the context small and makes the image's
# contents exactly what the COPY lines name.
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# `tests/` is excluded for the ordinary reason, and for one specific to this
# service: `tests/test_authority_matches_the_policy.py` reads
# `../policy-decision-service/pds/rules.py`, which is outside this build
# context and therefore unreadable in the image. That is the point -- see
# `scorer/authority.py`'s header. The image must carry the audit's own copy
# of the allowances and no route to the policy's.
tests/
